    {
      "slug": "po_22cdded5-2c5f-47e7-8b4e-16e2c155712a",
      "title": "Northern Lebanon 🇱🇧",
      "description": "After returning to Beirut on Dec 6, I travelled north to Tripoli. It's much cheaper than Beirut—in the souks, you could buy a kilogram of vibrant, ripe tomatoes for just £50,000 LBP ($0.56 USD).\n\nAfter, we headed up the mountain to Bcharre, where you can find Qadisha Valley and the Cedars of God. Perched upon a cliff is the Monastery of Mar Lishaa, with its many chapels cut into the rock face.",
